<body>
{{> cabecera_en 1=c}}
<main id="inicio">
<section class="portada solo">
<div class="envoltura">
<div>
<div class="eti">MTG Arena · Detailed Logs</div>
<h1>How to enable detailed logs in MTG Arena</h1>
<p class="sub">Detailed Logs is a setting in Arena. With it on, Arena writes every game to Player.log. Without it, Arena doesn&#x27;t write the games and a tracker cannot read your matches.</p>
<ol class="pasos-reg" id="pasos">
<li>In Arena, go to Options › Account.</li>
<li>Turn on «Detailed Logs (Plugin Support)».</li>
<li>Restart Arena.</li>
</ol>
<p class="ruta-completa">The option is at <span class="ruta">Options › Account › Detailed Logs (Plugin Support)</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="seccion franja" id="lee">
<div class="envoltura">
<div class="cab-sec">
<div class="eti">What it reads</div>
<h2>What ManaLab reads from the log, and what it doesn&#x27;t</h2>
</div>
<div class="mtgo-caja sola">
<h3>It reads</h3>
<ul>
<li><code>Player.log</code> and the card database Arena leaves on your PC, without changing them. <code>Player.log</code> is the file Arena writes when «Detailed Logs (Plugin Support)» is turned on in its settings.</li>
<li>Arena writes it to <code>C:\Users\&lt;your user&gt;\AppData\LocalLow\Wizards Of The Coast\MTGA\Player.log</code>.</li>
<li>ManaLab finds the log by itself. In Settings › Games you can set the path of Arena&#x27;s <code>Player.log</code>, only if it is not found automatically.</li>
</ul>
<h3>It doesn&#x27;t</h3>
<ul>
<li>It doesn&#x27;t modify Arena, doesn&#x27;t read its memory and doesn&#x27;t connect to Wizards&#x27; servers.</li>
<li>The optional overlay is a separate window that only shows public information or what can be worked out from what has been played, never hidden information.</li>
<li>Your games, screenshots and statistics stay in a folder on your PC, except what you share yourself: team mode, exporting a game or the AI analysis.</li>
</ul>
<p><a href="/safety/">Is ManaLab safe? What it reads and how to check it →</a></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="seccion" id="mtgo">
<div class="envoltura">
<div class="cab-sec">
<div class="eti">Magic Online</div>
<h2>And in Magic Online?</h2>
</div>
<div class="mtgo-caja sola">
<p>Magic Online needs no setting. It writes its own log, <code>mtgo.log</code>, with nothing to turn on: open Magic Online and ManaLab picks it up by itself.</p>
<p><a href="/magic-online/">ManaLab for Magic Online: what it saves and how it works →</a></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="seccion franja" id="siguiente">
<div class="envoltura">
<div class="apoyo uno">
<div>
<div class="eti">Next step</div>
<h2>Let ManaLab save your games</h2>
<p>ManaLab saves every match you play in MTG Arena and Magic Online on your PC and shows what works: your win rates by deck, by opponent and by matchup, your mulligans, your mistakes and your sideboard changes.</p>
<p>The app is free. Only the AI analysis is paid.</p>
